 34CL  H TYP=FUL$AUT=LIJIE SUN AND JUN CHEN$CIT=ENSDF$CUT=30-Sep-2026$          
 34CL  H TYP=FUL$AUT=NINEL NICA, BALRAJ SINGH$CIT=NDS 113, 1563 (2012)$         
 34CL2 H CUT=28-May-2012$                                                       
 34CL c  The isomeric transition of the {+34}Cl 146-keV metastable state.       
 34CL c  1980Wi13: {+34}Clm was produced via the {+31}P(|a,n) reaction with 10  
 34CL2c  and 11-MeV |a beams from the ONR-CIT tandem accelerator impinging on   
 34CL3c  MnP powder pressed in Be, Zr, and Al foils. |g rays were detected using
 34CL4c  a 100-cm{+3} Ge(Li) detector. Measured E|g, I|g. Deduced {+34}S levels,
 34CL5c  T{-1/2}, decay branching ratios, and log {Ift} for {+34}Cl{+m}|){+34}S 
 34CL6c  decay. Compared with shell-model calculations.                         
 34CL c  1975Va02: {+34}Cl{+m} was produced via the {+24}Mg({+12}C,pn) reaction 
 34CL2c  with a 35-MeV {+12}C beam from the Utrecht EN tandem accelerator. After
 34CL3c  one hour of bombardment, the radioactivity was detected using a        
 34CL4c  100-cm{+2} Ge(Li) detector and a 23|*28-cm{+2} NaI(Tl) detector for    
 34CL5c  Compton suppression. Measured E|g, I|g. Deduced levels, T{-1/2}, decay 
 34CL6c  branching ratios, and log {Ift} for {+34}Cl{+m}|){+34}S decay. Also    
 34CL7c  briefly reported {+34}Cl ground-state decay.                           
 34CL c  1983Kr06: {+34}Cl{+m} was produced via the {+35}Cl(p,pn) reaction with 
 34CL2c  25-MeV protons from the isochronous cyclotron of the Karlsruhe Research
 34CL3c  Center impinging on a NaCl target on a thin gold backing. Measured |b  
 34CL4c  spectra using the iron-free magnetic double-lens spectrometer. Deduced 
 34CL5c  end-point energies, |b-decay branching ratios, and Fermi and           
 34CL6c  Gamow-Teller shape factors.                                            
 34CL c  2006Ia05: Measured T{-1/2} at Cyclotron Institute, Texas A&M           
 34CL2c  University.                                                            
 34CL c  1983Ko22: {+12}C({+28}Si,3p3n) E=115 MeV at Chalk River. Tape transport
 34CL2c  system. 4|p proportional counter. Mass-separated sources. Measured     
 34CL3c  T{-1/2}.                                                               
 34CL c  1982Gr07: {+35}Cl(p,d) E=72 MeV at Schweizerisches Institut fur        
 34CL2c  Nuklearforschung (SIN) in Villigen, Switzerland. RbCl target. Ge(Li)   
 34CL3c  detector. Measured T{-1/2}.                                            
 34CL c  1973Ry01: {+31}P(|a,n|g) E=6.5, 6.65 MeV. Plastic scintillator,        
 34CL2c  multi-scaling decay spectra. Measured T{-1/2}, E|b, Q value.           
 34CL c  1972Ha82: {+32}S({+3}He,n) E=3.2 MeV. NE102 plastic scintillator.      
 34CL2c  Measured T{-1/2}, E|b.                                                 
 34CL c  1971Sn01: {+32}S({+3}He,p|g) E=6.8 MeV. Measured E|g, I|g, DSAM        
 34CL c  1971Wa04: {+35}Cl(n,2n|g){+34}Cl E=14.8 MeV. Ge(Li), NaI(Tl), and      
 34CL2c  plastic detectors. Measured T{-1/2}, E|g, I|g, E|b, I|b.               
 34CL c  1965Eb01: {+35}Cl(n,2n|g){+34}Cl E=14.7 MeV, natural target, NaI(Tl)   
 34CL2c  detectors. Measured T{-1/2}.                                           
